alysis","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Fantasy","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 10 NFL highlights: Best plays, moments, touchdowns, more","description":"Check here for all of Sunday's top moments, TDs and analysis from ESPN's NFL reporters.","published":"2026-11-16T05:24:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50489998/week-10-highlights-sunday-best-plays-touchdowns-2026","type":"Story","byline":"NFL Nation","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Aaron Rodgers makes fantasy football history, now No. 2 on all-time scoring list","description":"With Aaron Rodgers' score on Sunday, he reaches another fantasy football accolade in his HOF-worthy career.","published":"2026-11-16T04:27:04.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50328859/fantasy-football-aaron-rodgers-career-points-scoring","type":"Story","byline":"Tristan H. Cockcroft","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"49ers put up big numbers vs. Cowboys, tout 'incredibly dangerous' offense","description":"The 49ers racked up 584 yards against the Cowboys on Sunday in a jaw-dropping offensive display led by Brock Purdy, Christian McCaffrey and Deebo Samuel.","published":"2026-11-16T05:29:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50498373/49ers-put-big-numbers-victory-cowboys","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Nick Wagoner","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Trevor Nowaske","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevor_Nowaske","description":"American football player (born 1998)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:35:28Z","intro":"Trevor Nowaske (born November 7, 1998) is an American professional football linebacker for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Saginaw Valley State Cardinals. He signed with the Detroit Lions as an undrafted free agent in 2023.","sections":[{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"DETROIT LIONS\nOn May 12, 2023, the Detroit Lions signed Nowaske to a three-year, $2.695 million contract as an undrafted free agent. He was waived by Detroit on August 29, and was re-signed to the team's practice squad. On November 2, Nowaske was signed to the active roster. He was waived by the Lions on December 28.\n\nARIZONA CARDINALS\nOn December 29, 2023, Nowaske was claimed off waivers by the Arizona Cardinals. He was waived by the Cardinals on August 27, 2024.\n\nDETROIT LIONS (SECOND STINT)\nOn August 28, 2024, the Detroit Lions claimed Nowaske off waivers. On October 27 against the Tennessee Titans, Nowaske recorded his first interception off of Mason Rudolph.\nOn March 14, 2025, Nowaske re-signed with the Lions.\nOn March 16, 2026, Nowaske re-signed with the Lions."}],"wikidataId":"Q121461325","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-03-13","text":"Signed DB Izien Christian and LB Trevor Nowaske to contracts."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/5144894","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/N/NowaTr00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/trevor-nowaske/169859","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/trevor-nowaske/11481","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevor_Nowaske"},"insights":["Ranks 1st of 80 qualified linebackers in completion % allowed.","Ranks 2nd of 80 qualified linebackers in passer rating allowed.","On the field for 28% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.4M is the 29th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season."]}